# Change-Impact Review Mandate

A code / config / IaC / script / interface / doc / structure change is NOT
complete until you have reviewed what downstream surfaces it may have made
stale. Green tests are NOT "done" — the repository's own documentation and
toolchain standards drift silently while every test passes.

## When (self-gating — neither skip nor rubber-stamp)

At completion of any MEANINGFUL change. A pure-internal refactor with no
plausible downstream surface → record `none — <one-line reason>` and move on.
Do NOT manufacture a decision when there is genuinely no impacted surface; do
NOT skip the review when there is one.

## How

Consult `.ai/harness/context/change-impact-map.md` for your CHANGE-TYPE, then
act per affected SURFACE-CLASS.

### Documentation surface-class → explicit DECISION (exactly one)

- **update-required** — a doc / README / guide / `.env.example` / example /
  behavior-comment now contradicts reality; fix before declaring done.
- **update-recommended** — stale-ish but non-blocking; note it.
- **none** — no doc impact; state the REASON (one line, mandatory).
- **ADR-worthy** — an architectural/operational DECISION was made → capture via
  `cbharness-capture-adr` (an ADR, NEVER a lesson).
- **harness-context-update** — DDD / `.ai/harness/context/` / a rule is now stale.
- **local-skill-or-rule-update** — a repeated operation or new constraint emerged.

Doc surfaces include: `README.md`, `docs/`, architecture/guides/maintainer docs,
`.ai/harness/adrs/`, DDD files, `.ai/harness/context/`, root `AGENTS.md`/
`CLAUDE.md`, examples/templates, behavior-documenting comments, `.env.example`.

### Toolchain / consistency surface-class → run the GOVERNING CHECK

If the change touches files governed by a discovered toolchain surface
(`.editorconfig`, markdown/prettier/eslint/ruff/black/shellcheck/tflint config,
`.gitignore`/nested `.gitignore`/`.gitattributes`, version files such as
`.tool-versions`/`.terraform-version`), RUN that surface's recorded check — do
NOT rely only on the obvious test/formatter. A change is not consistent with the
repo until it passes the repo's OWN declared standards. New generated artifacts →
cross-check `.gitignore`/`.gitattributes` intent (tracked vs ignored on purpose).

## Discovered, never invented

The change-impact map is built from ACTUAL repository files (Phase 0.3a
discovery). NEVER invent a markdown / Terraform / lint / CI / IDE convention no
repo file declares. Absent surface = absent; do not fabricate a standard.

## Non-Negotiable

- NEVER declare a change "done" on green tests alone while a mapped surface is stale.
- NEVER record a `none` documentation decision without a one-line reason.
- NEVER skip the governing toolchain check for a change-type the map covers.
- A stale doc or a skipped lint/format/version check after a change is a
  first-class defect — surfaced at session-end by `codebase-harness-reflect`
  (Surface-Impact friction), never silent debt.